@startuml 18-seq-report-review
!include ../../_style.iuml
title Nós no Cabo v1 — Reports and review by email

actor Visitor
participant "SPA\nReportDialog" as spa
participant "catalog" as catalog
database "catalog D1" as db
participant "Email Routing" as mail <<external>>
actor "Reviewer" as reviewer

== Report ==
Visitor -> spa : "Notificar problema"\n(reason, optional comment)
spa -> catalog : POST /v1/websites/:id/reports\n+ Turnstile (via gateway)
catalog -> db : insert reports (one per reporter_ip_hash),\nreview_flag = reported
catalog -> mail : report alert from ALERT_FROM to ALERT_TO,\nReply-To alertas+<id>.<HMAC>@nosnocabo.com.br
catalog --> spa : 202
note right of db
  A report never hides the site:
  it stays published until reviewed.
end note

== Review ==
mail -> reviewer : alert email
reviewer -> mail : reply, first line:\n"dismiss" | "ban [unsafe|unreachable|error]"
mail -> catalog : email() handler
catalog -> catalog : accept only mail from ALERT_TO\nwith a valid signed Reply-To
alt dismiss
  catalog -> db : published, review_flag = NULL,\nreports deleted (publishes a held site)
else ban
  catalog -> db : rejected with the reason
end
catalog -> catalog : push to the submitter, if subscribed
catalog -> mail : confirmation reply
mail -> reviewer : confirmation

note over catalog
  Moderation alerts (new site published, rejected
  or held) use the same signed Reply-To, so a held
  site is reviewed the same way. The review script in
  the private moderation repo does the same over D1.
end note

@enduml
